  "description" : "An addon for 10 weapons for Feast of Fire and Flames from the firearms companies Harrington and Richardson and Stevens Arms, 5 each\nThe weapons are not balanced and have accurate damage (based on how FFS calculates damage with round weight and velocity) to their real ammunition performance.\nAll items can be bought from Papachino in the shuttle, load order has been fixed so this works now\nAll weapons reworked for FFS 2.0 weapon changes\n\n[h1] H&R [/h1]\nStarting in 1871 as Wesson & Harrington in Worcester Massachusetts, H&R produced a number of firearms of different kinds including the first revolver with an extractor, being eventually bought out by Remington.\n\n[u] 2 Revolvers [/u]\n[b] \"H&R .22 Special\" [/b]\nActually referring to a number of revolvers, the mod represents a 6\" barreled variant.\nitemID : \"ffs_22special_1\"\n.22 LR 9 shot revolver\n-custom animation\n-custom sound\n-custom lua\n\n[b] \"H&R Model 925 'Defender'\" [/b]\nVisually similar to the 22 Special, but with shorter barrel lengths and a .38 caliber 5 shot cylinder.\nitemID : \"ffs_defender_1\"\n.38 Special 5 shot revolver\n-custom animation\n-custom sound\n-custom lua\n\n[u] 1 Semi-Auto Pistol [/u]\n[b] \"H&R Self-Loading Pistol\" [/b]\nModified from the .25 caliber version designed by Webley, improving the pistol and increasing its caliber.\n.32 ACP 8 round pistol\nitemID : \"ffs_selfloading_1\"\n-custom animation\n\n[u]1 Handgun [/u]\n[b] \"H&R Handygun\" [/b]\n.410 Bore 000 Buck smooth bore handgun\nThe smooth bore version of the H&R Handygun, produced with both rifled and smooth bore barrels. Classified as \"any other weapon\" due to being a stockless shotgun.\nitemID : \"ffs_handygun_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom sound\n-custom lua\n-custom ammo properties\n\n[u] 1 Submachinegun [/u]\n[b] \"M50 Reising\" [/b]\nA lighter, cheaper, more accurate competitor for the Thompson, designed by Reising who worked as an assistant to Browning. Designed as a police weapon, its civilian grade construction limited its use to only the USMC during WWII. The weapon had its charging handle in the weapon's forearm as shown in the reload and draw animation\n.45 ACP 500rpm submachinegun\nitem ID : \"ffs_reising_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom sound\n\n\n[h1] Stevens Arms [/h1]\nFounded by Joshua Stevens in 1864 in Chicopee Falls, Massachusetts, produced mostly sporting arms, introduced the 22 LR round, and eventually bought by Westinghouse and then Savage Arms. Once contracted to produce Mosin-Nagants, most of which were not delivered and sold to the US government.\n\n[u] 1 Singleshot Target Pistol [/u]\n[b] \"Lord No 36\" [/b]\n.32 Long Colt tipup singleshot pistol\nOne of three models of target pistol named after famous marksmen of the time, the Lord was the most popular of the three. 2 custom pistols were ordered by Buffalo Bill for himself and Ben Thompson.\nitemID : \"ffs_lord_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom sound\n-custom lua\n\n[u] 3 Singleshot Rifles [/u]\n[b] \"Stevens Arms' Marksman'\" [/b]\nA small caliber target rifle, one of the many rifles produced by Stevens cheaper than Winchester at similar quality making them competitive.\n.22 LR tipup singleshot rifle\nitemID : \"ffs_marksman_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom lua\n\n[b] \"Stevens Arms 'Favorite'\" [/b]\nA targeting rifle using a tiltblock breech, also produced chambered for Stevens' own .25 caliber round. A \"tiltblock\" is a falling block with a breech block that pivots instead of sliding vertically. Depicted in the mod with a folding long range rear iron sigt to differentiate it visually from the other 2 Stevens rifles. \n.25-20 WCF tiltblock singleshot rifle\nitemID : \"ffs_favorite_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom lua\n\n[b] \"Stevens Arms 'Ideal' 44\" [/b]\nBasically a larger, sturdier Favorite, with the version chambered for the .44-40 Winchester being the largest variant produced. Depicted in the mod with a 19th century style scope to differentiate it visually from the other 2 Stevens rifles. \n.45-40 WCF tiltblock singleshot rifle\nitemID : \"ffs_ideal44_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom lua\n\nThe Favorite and the Ideal are very visually similar and I saw images with both sights on them so I just made the two with these sights to make the two unique at a glance from each other and the Marksman.\n\n[u] 1 Pump-action Shotgun [/u]\n[b] \"M520-30 Trenchgun\" [/b]\nA pump action shotgun produced by Stevens prior to WWII as the M520 and M520A and later modified with a heat shield, bayonet bracket, and slam fire action for military use and designated the M520-30 trench gun. The slam fire action is the difference between classifying a shotgun as a trench gun or not. The weapon was in use through the Vietnam war.\n12 Gauge 00 Buck pump action shotgun\nitemID : \"ffs_m520_1\"\n-custom animation\n-custom ammo properties",
